  "oracle_review": [
    "All133 test lines reread. Four Unit-returning @Test methods exercise English/Arabic at density1 and font scales1/2 with the real MafiaSetupScreen constrained to320x640dp.",
    "The localized action descriptions identify each real icon button. Label selection is bound to the exact layout parent of its controls group, avoiding the duplicate English Mafia title. This ancestry is true under both old Row and new FlowRow; RED02 failures are actual width assertions, not selector errors.",
    "SemanticsNode.size is used for un-clipped measured layout geometry, so inflated touch bounds cannot hide a0/7/19/41px button. density1 makes48px the production48dp minimum from ParlorIconButton/ParlorSpacing.xxl.",
    "Each nonzero button is individually scrolled into view before clipped/unclipped bounds are compared; scrolling a shorter label alone is not treated as proof that its taller control is visible. Assertions also reject screen overflow and overlap with label or sibling.",
    "Zero-width controls are not silently skipped: the48px assertion still fails. A scroll attempt is skipped only for zero geometry to avoid masking the width witness with an unrelated scroll exception.",
    "All three role steppers and the separate Maximum revotes stepper are checked, including the valid disabled decrement for Mafia count1. The regression intentionally tests layout, not click dispatch or every possible viewport/font scale."
  ],
  "compatibility_and_regression_review": [
    "Diff changes only FlowRow import and outer layout/vertical arrangement. Child icons, localized names, callbacks, enabling conditions, count formatting, role-count bounds, shared controls, and state ownership are unchanged.",
    "Reread SetupDraft: Doctor repeat-protection flag, self-heal flag, defaults, and compatibility-only timer fields are preserved by applyTo. No protocol, serialized settings, snapshot, reducer or role-projection change.",
    "Reread MafiaActionAuthority classification and reducer setup guards: ConfigureAndStart remains host-only and is validated atomically in Setup. Local/LAN authority is not bypassed by the layout change.",
    "Siblings inspected: weighted-label ToggleRow remains intact; RuleChoiceCard and derived civilian read-only row are unaffected. No Whodunit or generic networking/session file appears in the diff.",
    "Wrapping increases content height deliberately; the existing verticalScroll container owns the overflow. No fixed height, smaller text, ellipsis, hard-coded LTR placement, or accessibility suppression was introduced."
  ],
